{"nodes": [{"id": "references_workflow", "label": "references/workflow.md (Role Protocols)", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "handyman/references/workflow.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "references_workflow", "label": "Harness Workflow", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "handyman/references/workflow.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "references_workflow_stages", "label": "Seven-Stage Feature Lifecycle", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "handyman/references/workflow.md", "source_location": "Stages at a Glance", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Each stage (0-6 plus period close 7) has a deterministic guardian and leaves a dated artifact on disk; measures are derived from artifacts, never declared in the contract. Rule: a stage without its artifact did not happen."}, {"id": "references_workflow_bootstrap_protocol", "label": "Bootstrap Protocol", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "handyman/references/workflow.md", "source_location": "Bootstrap Protocol", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Run the scaffold first and always; hand-creating files is the main source of cross-model drift. The business interview is mandatory because the domain lives in the user's head, unlike architecture and conventions which can be read from code."}, {"id": "references_workflow_leader_protocol", "label": "Leader Protocol", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "handyman/references/workflow.md", "source_location": "Leader Protocol", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The leader coordinates, never implements product code, and never marks a feature done alone; it runs the strongest model and widest tools and delegates bounded work to cheaper roles."}, {"id": "references_workflow_implementer_protocol", "label": "Implementer Protocol", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "handyman/references/workflow.md", "source_location": "Implementer Protocol", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "references_workflow_reviewer_protocol", "label": "Reviewer Protocol", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "handyman/references/workflow.md", "source_location": "Reviewer Protocol", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Review runs in two ordered stages (spec compliance, then code quality); a Stage 1 failure reports CHANGES_REQUESTED immediately so spec drift is never buried under style feedback. The reviewer never edits product code."}, {"id": "references_workflow_closure_protocol", "label": "Closure Protocol", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "handyman/references/workflow.md", "source_location": "Closure Protocol", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "A feature closes only with green verifier, approval, and both reports on disk; post_run hooks run with exit 0 always so a failing custom step only warns and never reverts a verified close."}, {"id": "references_workflow_unattended_loop", "label": "Unattended Loop (ralph loop)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "handyman/references/workflow.md", "source_location": "Unattended Loop", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Handyman deliberately ships no runner: the loop is the operator's responsibility; the harness contributes the contract that makes looping safe (feature ready exit 3 as stop signal, single in_progress invariant, verifier gate)."}, {"id": "references_workflow_sprint_protocol", "label": "Sprint Protocol", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "handyman/references/workflow.md", "source_location": "Sprint Protocol", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "A sprint is a partition label, not a date; the sprint document's derived sections are regenerated at close from artifacts stages 0-6 already left, never hand-maintained, because a hand-kept copy of state is exactly the drift the harness exists to avoid."}, {"id": "references_workflow_parallel_exploration", "label": "Parallel Exploration (explorer subagents)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "handyman/references/workflow.md", "source_location": "Parallel Exploration", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Each explorer gets one narrow question, the cheapest model, a read-only tool set, and returns only a file reference; the leader synthesizes reports before selecting implementation scope."}, {"id": "references_workflow_stability_check", "label": "Stability Check (preflight)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "handyman/references/workflow.md", "source_location": "Stability check before feature work", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "preflight.js orchestrates six controls (format, contract, version drift, config-role sync, discovery, worklist) but always exits 0: it reports stability rather than gating, because the blocking checks already live in the verifier's validate phase."}], "edges": [{"source": "references_workflow", "target": "references_workflow_stages", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "handyman/references/workflow.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "references_workflow", "target": "references_workflow_bootstrap_protocol", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "handyman/references/workflow.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "references_workflow", "target": "references_workflow_leader_protocol", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "handyman/references/workflow.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "references_workflow", "target": "references_workflow_implementer_protocol", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "handyman/references/workflow.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "references_workflow", "target": "references_workflow_reviewer_protocol", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "handyman/references/workflow.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "references_workflow", "target": "references_workflow_closure_protocol", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "handyman/references/workflow.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "references_workflow", "target": "references_workflow_unattended_loop", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "handyman/references/workflow.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "references_workflow", "target": "references_workflow_sprint_protocol", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "handyman/references/workflow.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "references_workflow", "target": "references_workflow_parallel_exploration", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "handyman/references/workflow.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "references_workflow", "target": "references_workflow_stability_check", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "handyman/references/workflow.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "references_workflow", "target": "references_security